 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "64:8-11 is not glossed (Al-Muyassar's «لا يخلف الله وعده» is 30:6 word for word). 65:1-3 addresses the Prophet ﷺ: no motif there. Light for «لا خوف عليهم» and «لهم البشرى», geometric for «إن العزة لله جميعا», stars for the heavens, wind for «إن يتبعون إلا الظن». STAGING v4: c1 (62-64): the allies of Allah are the believers who fear Him (63; Al-Muyassar: obeying His commands and avoiding His prohibitions): four believers (men in light robes) in a prayer hall at dawn. A light plate for no fear on them (62:6 to 63:1, starting 3 s after the Name); they pray from 63:2 (they believed and were God-fearing): ruku, rising, two prostrations with the sitting between, then they stand (64:12); plates fade while they pray, and nobody prays toward a plate or a person. After the prayer a growth plate for the great attainment (64:14) and a soft sparkle on them (64:15). Nothing of the Hereafter or of Paradise is drawn for 64:6-7. c2 (65) stays ambient (geometric): it consoles the Prophet ﷺ himself (his grief at their words: his own state is never staged), then Allah's might, hearing and knowledge; params.quiet over 65:1-3; a geometric plate for all might belongs to Allah (65:4-7). c3 (66), split from c2 at the verse boundary with a new title: the polytheists who invoke partners, three faceless men in dark robes in a town by day; a stars plate for those in the heavens (66:5-9, gone before 66:16); the camera on them as they follow (66:11) and on their partners besides Allah (66:18); no idol is drawn and nobody turns toward an empty side; a wind plate for they follow only conjecture (66:19-21); they speak on 66:25 (they only lie: the gloss frames it)."
 },
